# =============================================================================
# SNHS ID Studio - environment variables
# =============================================================================
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the value:
#     cp .env.example .env.local
#
# .env and .env.* are gitignored (.env.example is the one exception).
# Never commit a file containing a real token.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT DOES *NOT* BELONG HERE
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Apps Script webhook URL, the Google Sheet link and the school branding all
# live in js/config.js. That file is downloaded by every visitor's browser, so
# nothing in it is secret -- and moving it here would not make it secret either,
# because the browser still needs it. Only values used by server-side code in
# api/ can be kept private, which today means the single token below.
#
# Staff passwords are not here either: they live in the Staff_Accounts tab of
# the Google Sheet, so they can be changed without a redeploy.
#
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN  (required only for student photo storage)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read/write token for the Vercel Blob store that holds student ID photos.
# Read server-side only, by api/upload-photo.js -- it never reaches the browser.
#
# ON VERCEL: you do not set this by hand. Connect a Blob store to the project
# and Vercel injects it into every deployment automatically:
#     Vercel dashboard -> Storage -> Create Database -> Blob
#                      -> Connect Project -> select this project
#
# LOCALLY: pull the value Vercel generated for you:
#     npx vercel link
#     npx vercel env pull .env.local
#
# Or copy it from the Blob store's ".env.local" tab in the dashboard.
# The value looks like: vercel_blob_rw_AbCdEf123456_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
#
# If this is unset the app still works: api/upload-photo.js returns 501, the
# browser falls back to keeping the photo locally, and registration continues.
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=
